      "worked": "The smaller angle between the ground bearings is\n$$\\begin{align*}\\angle AOB&=(360^\\circ-310^\\circ)+65^\\circ\\\\\\angle AOB&=115^\\circ\\end{align*}$$\nFrom $\\triangle OAC$, let $a=OA$:\n$$\\begin{align*}\\tan40^\\circ&=\\frac{25}{a}\\\\a&=\\frac{25}{\\tan40^\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nLet $b=OB$. Apply the cosine rule in $\\triangle OAB$:\n$$\\begin{align*}70^2&=a^2+b^2-2ab\\cos115^\\circ\\\\b^2-2a\\cos115^\\circ\\,b+a^2-4900&=0\\\\b&=a\\cos115^\\circ+\\sqrt{4900-a^2\\sin^2115^\\circ}\\end{align*}$$\nThe other quadratic root is negative, so it cannot represent a distance. Using the exact expression for $a$, from $\\triangle OBD$:\n$$\\begin{align*}h&=b\\tan30^\\circ\\\\h&\\approx30.0\\,\\mathrm{m}\\end{align*}$$",
